    b: { label: 'The town.', key: 'town', text: 'You go to the slope. Your team holds it for the hour it takes to empty the lower street, and when it finally goes, it buries nothing but gardens. Up at the mine they dig with their hands. The shift comes out at dusk, all twelve, alive, some of them carried. One will not work underground again. He tells you it is all right. He says he was thinking of stopping anyway.', together: 'You and your ally run for the slope together. The quake has driven everything out of the hillside and down toward the town.' },
    split: { text: 'Three down the mine. Three across the slope. You stand at the adit mouth where you can hear the tapping and see the hill, and you call both ways until your voice goes. If both halves hold, the shift comes up and the slope stays put.', foe: 'The Aftershock', sprite: 'onix', types: ['rock', 'ground'], won: 'You held the slope and emptied the mine in the same hour. Nobody was under either', lost: 'You tried to hold the slope and empty the mine at once, and one of them fell' },
